msgid "Guida"
msgstr "Guide"

#: services/guides.py:99
msgid "llms.txt: guida pratica per la citabilità IA"
msgstr "llms.txt: practical guide for AI citability"

#: services/guides.py:101
msgid ""
"Cos’è llms.txt, come strutturarlo per AIO/GEO e come Centropic lo genera e lo"
" valida nel crawl."
msgstr ""
"What is llms.txt, how to structure it for AIO/GEO, and how Centropic "
"generates and validates it in the crawl."

#: services/guides.py:104
msgid ""
"Un file root machine-readable che spiega brand, topic e pagine preferite ai "
"modelli e crawler AI."
msgstr ""
"A machine-readable root file that explains brand, topics, and preferred pages"
" to AI models and crawlers."

#: services/guides.py:107
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Perché conta</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">llms.txt riduce ambiguità entity: dice chi sei, cosa "
"offri e quali URL citare. In Centropic la presenza e la qualità del file "
"alimentano score AIO/GEO (probe Misurato).</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Answer engine e crawler AI (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, "
"PerplexityBot, Google-Extended) usano segnali pubblici; un llms.txt chiaro è "
"un’ancora di citazione accanto a Schema.org e robots permissivi.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Sezioni utili</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Site / Summary / Key topics con brand e dominio canonici</li>\n"
"      <li>Preferred citation (brand + acronimi espansi: AIO, GEO)</li>\n"
"      <li>Important pages con URL https assoluti</li>\n"
"      <li>Disambiguazione (cosa non siete: GIS, All-in-One generici)</li>\n"
"      <li>Contact e owner / parent organization</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Come Centropic aiuta</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Ogni analisi genera una bozza <code>llms.txt</code> nel"
" pack HTML unico. Pubblicala in root "
"(<code>https://tuodominio/llms.txt</code>) e ri-analizza: il finding passa a "
"“disponibile” se il probe la trova.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Esempio vivo: il llms.txt di Centropic è su <a "
"href=\"/llms.txt\">centropic.ai/llms.txt</a>, con preferred citation e link a"
" metodologia.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Checklist rapida</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Una sola brand primaria (evita nomi fantasma)</li>\n"
"      <li>URL canonici https, niente query di tracking</li>\n"
"      <li>Allinea llms.txt a JSON-LD Organization e alla home</li>\n"
"      <li>Aggiorna la data quando cambi offerta o positioning</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Vedi anche <a href=\"/guide/schema-ai\">Schema AI</a> e"
" <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Why it matters</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">llms.txt reduces entity ambiguity: it tells who you "
"are, what you offer, and which URLs to cite. In Centropic, the presence and "
"quality of the file feed AIO/GEO scores (Measured probe).</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Answer engines and AI crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, "
"PerplexityBot, Google-Extended) use public signals; a clear llms.txt is a "
"citation anchor alongside Schema.org and permissive robots.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Useful sections</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Site / Summary / Key topics with canonical brand and domain</li>\n"
"      <li>Preferred citation (brand + expanded acronyms: AIO, GEO)</li>\n"
"      <li>Important pages with absolute https URLs</li>\n"
"      <li>Disambiguation (what you are not: GIS, generic All-in-One)</li>\n"
"      <li>Contact and owner / parent organization</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">How Centropic helps</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Every analysis generates a draft <code>llms.txt</code> "
"in the single HTML pack. Publish it at root "
"(<code>https://yourdomain/llms.txt</code>) and re-analyze: the finding turns "
"“available” once the probe finds it.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Live example: Centropic's own llms.txt is at <a "
"href=\"/llms.txt\">centropic.ai/llms.txt</a>, with preferred citation and a "
"link to the methodology.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Quick checklist</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>One single primary brand (avoid ghost names)</li>\n"
"      <li>Canonical https URLs, no tracking queries</li>\n"
"      <li>Align llms.txt with the JSON-LD Organization and the homepage</li>\n"
"      <li>Update the date whenever you change your offer or positioning</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">See also <a href=\"/guide/schema-ai\">Schema AI</a> and"
" the <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"

#: services/guides.py:147
msgid "Schema.org per answer engine (AIO/GEO)"
msgstr "Schema.org for answer engine (AIO/GEO)"

#: services/guides.py:149
msgid ""
"Quali tipi Schema.org aiutano AI-Driven Visibility e Generative Engine "
"Optimization: Organization, WebSite, FAQPage, SoftwareApplication, Article."
msgstr ""
"Which Schema.org types help AI-Driven Visibility and Generative Engine "
"Optimization: Organization, WebSite, FAQPage, SoftwareApplication, Article."

#: services/guides.py:152
msgid ""
"I dati strutturati non “garantiscono” citazioni, ma rendono l’entity "
"leggibile a crawler e modelli. Aggiornato 30/07/2026."
msgstr ""
"Structured data does not 'guarantee' citations, but makes the entity readable"
" to crawlers and models. Updated 30/07/2026."

#: services/guides.py:155
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Tipi prioritari</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li><strong>Organization</strong> + <strong>WebSite</strong> collegati "
"via @id</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>FAQPage</strong> per Q&amp;A tipizzate allineate all’HTML "
"visibile</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>SoftwareApplication</strong> o Product se vendi software "
"(come Centropic)</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>Article</strong> / HowTo per guide evergreen con author e "
"date</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Riferimento normativo: <a href=\"https://schema.org/\" "
"rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">schema.org</a>. In Centropic i "
"tipi rilevati alimentano score AIO/GEO (probe Misurato).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Errori comuni</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">JSON-LD orfano senza tipi chiave, sameAs solo self-"
"referenziali, FAQ senza acceptedAnswer, Organization senza contatto o logo. "
"Centropic li segnala nei findings.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Un sameAs verso il solo sito proprietario non basta: "
"preferisci profili esterni reali (azienda madre, directory, social "
"verificati).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Checklist minima</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>name + url + email (o telephone) su Organization</li>\n"
"      <li>sameAs verso profili esterni reali (non pagine interne del "
"sito)</li>\n"
"      <li>logo ImageObject con URL assoluto https e caption</li>\n"
"      <li>FAQPage solo se le domande sono visibili in pagina</li>\n"
"      <li>knowsAbout allineato a llms.txt e al copy della home</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Vedi anche <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a>, <a"
" href=\"/guide/llms-txt\">llms.txt</a> e <a href=\"/guide/score-vs-"
"sov\">score vs SoV</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"<section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Priority types</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li><strong>Organization</strong> + <strong>WebSite</strong> linked via"
" @id</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>FAQPage</strong> for Q&amp;A types aligned with visible "
"HTML</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>SoftwareApplication</strong> or Product if you sell "
"software (like Centropic)</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>Article</strong> / HowTo for evergreen guides with author "
"and date</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Regulatory reference: <a href=\"https://schema.org/\" "
"rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">schema.org</a>. In Centropic, "
"the detected types feed AIO/GEO scores (Measured probe).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Common errors</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Orphan JSON-LD without key types, sameAs only self-"
"referential, FAQ without acceptedAnswer, Organization without contact or "
"logo. Centropic flags these in the findings.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">A sameAs pointing to only the proprietary site is not "
"enough: prefer real external profiles (parent company, directories, verified "
"social).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Minimum checklist</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>name + url + email (or telephone) on Organization</li>\n"
"      <li>sameAs pointing to real external profiles (not internal site "
"pages)</li>\n"
"      <li>logo ImageObject with absolute https URL and caption</li>\n"
"      <li>FAQPage only if questions are visible on the page</li>\n"
"      <li>knowsAbout aligned with llms.txt and the homepage copy</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">See also <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a>, <a "
"href=\"/guide/llms-txt\">llms.txt</a>, and <a href=\"/guide/score-vs-"
"sov\">score vs SoV</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>"

#: services/guides.py:191
msgid "CVI, score AIO/GEO e citation share"
msgstr "AIO/GEO score and SoV"

#: services/guides.py:193
msgid ""
"Centropic Visibility Index (CVI) vs sotto-score AIO/GEO e citation share "
"campionata (SoV proxy/measured)."
msgstr ""
"Centropic Visibility Index (CVI) vs. AIO/GEO subscores and sampled citation "
"share (SoV proxy/measured)."

#: services/guides.py:196
msgid ""
"Tre livelli: CVI (standard proprietario), AIO/GEO (componenti), citation "
"share (campione stocastico sulle risposte)."
msgstr ""
"Three layers: CVI (proprietary standard), AIO/GEO (components), citation "
"share (stochastic sample of responses)."

#: services/guides.py:199
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Centropic Visibility Index (CVI)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Il <strong>CVI</strong> è la metrica di categoria di "
"Centropic: 0–100 + lettera DDD→AAA. Riassume predisposizione strutturale "
"(AIO+GEO) con penalità findings. È ciò che confronti tra brand, competitor e "
"nel tempo.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Score AIO / GEO (componenti)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Sotto-score 0–100 da crawl e probe. Badge Stimato sul "
"compositario; i check di presenza file possono essere Misurato.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>AIO (AI-Driven Visibility)</strong> premia "
"leggibilità per sistemi IA: entity, schema, FAQ, llms.txt, meta. <strong>GEO "
"(Generative Engine Optimization)</strong> premia citabilità e policy crawler "
"AI.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Citation share (non SoV "
"pubblicitaria)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Nei media tradizionali “Share of Voice” conta "
"impression e PR. Qui misuriamo <strong>menzioni in risposte "
"generative</strong> — stocastiche, prompt-dipendenti. In UI resta l’etichetta"
" SoV per continuità; in metodologia è citation share.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>Proxy</strong>: formula su AIO/GEO + robots. "
"<strong>Measured</strong> (Plus/Business): campioni prompt su LLM con "
"conteggio menzioni brand. Non confondere i due.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Come leggerli insieme</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Alza il <strong>CVI</strong> chiudendo i gap AIO/GEO: "
"l’IA non cita ciò che non legge. Poi campiona la citation share. CVI alto = "
"controllo del dato; measured = campione sulle risposte.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Centropic mostra sempre l’evidence badge: Stimato, "
"Misto o Misurato. Dettagli in <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a> e nel "
"prodotto su <a href=\"/prodotto\">/prodotto</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Score AIO / GEO</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">0–100 indexes from crawl and probes. Estimated badge on"
" the composite; individual file-presence checks can be Measured.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>AIO (AI-Driven Visibility)</strong> rewards "
"readability for AI systems: entity, schema, FAQ, llms.txt, meta. <strong>GEO "
"(Generative Engine Optimization)</strong> rewards citability and AI crawler "
"policy.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Share of Voice (SoV)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>Proxy</strong>: a formula on AIO/GEO + observed"
" robots. <strong>Measured</strong>: prompt polling on LLMs (Plus/Business) "
"counting brand mentions. Do not confuse the two.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">To raise measured SoV: strengthen your public entity "
"(llms.txt, Organization, about), publish citable content, and expand the "
"prompt bank with the questions your market actually asks.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">How to read them together</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Raise the signals first (score), then measure the voice"
" (SoV). A high SoV with a low score is fragile; a high score without measured"
" SoV remains a diagnosis, not proof of citation.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Centropic always shows the evidence badge: Estimated, "
"Mixed, or Measured. Details in the <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a> "
"and in the product at <a href=\"/prodotto\">/prodotto</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"

